import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — the enumerate arm's attr gap: instantiation reach, fixed","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — the enumerate arm's attr gap: instantiation reach, fixed","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/enum-attr-gap.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/enum-attr-gap.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/enum-attr-gap.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-the-enumerate-arm-s-attr-gap-instantiation-reach-fixed" tabindex="-1">Retro — the enumerate arm&#39;s attr gap: instantiation reach, fixed <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-enumerate-arm-s-attr-gap-instantiation-reach-fixed" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the enumerate arm&#39;s attr gap: instantiation reach, fixed”">​</a></h1><p>Date: 2026-10-15 (follow-up to <code>exposed-math.md</code>) Context: the exposure retro measured the enumerate arm at <strong>0 fires across 8 models</strong> (~1,263 candidates) and diagnosed an attr gap — the enumerator mints <code>select X</code> while real exports carry <code>select(x, dim=1, index=0)</code>. This change fixes the machinery and re-measures on the same slice.</p><h2 id="the-actual-defect-was-two-defects" tabindex="-1">The actual defect was two defects <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-actual-defect-was-two-defects" aria-label="Permalink to “The actual defect was two defects”">​</a></h2><p>The retro named the attr gap. Reproducing it showed a second, equally fatal one underneath:</p><ol><li><strong>Attr-free patterns.</strong> <code>_term_match</code> / the compiled <code>_POp</code> matcher require exact attr-key-set equality — <code>set(term.attrs) == set(pat.attrs)</code>. <code>select X</code> never matches <code>select(x, dim=1, index=0)</code>.</li><li><strong>Concrete <code>Var</code> leaves.</strong> <code>enumerate_candidates</code> instantiated metas to <code>Var(&quot;A&quot;, (4,4))</code> inside <code>Candidate.lhs</code>, and <code>as_rule()</code> shipped those leaves into the <code>Rewrite</code>. A <code>Var</code> in a pattern compiles to <code>_PLeaf</code> — keyed by <code>repr</code>, matching only the enumerator&#39;s own instance. Even an attr-free <code>add A B</code> candidate could fire nowhere but at its own root — which is why <code>verify_law</code>/<code>_cost_delta</code> &quot;worked&quot; (the own-instance fire) while <code>impact._probe</code> on real terms saw zero.</li></ol><p>So the enumerator was doubly synthetic: evaluated on instances only it could see.</p><h2 id="the-fix-—-two-forms-per-candidate" tabindex="-1">The fix — two forms per candidate <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-fix-—-two-forms-per-candidate" aria-label="Permalink to “The fix — two forms per candidate”">​</a></h2><p><code>enumerate_candidates</code> now mints, per rewriting-form pair:</p><ul><li>the <strong>evaluated instance</strong> (<code>Candidate.lhs</code>/<code>rhs</code>) — <code>Var</code>/<code>Const</code> leaves plus a concrete attr draw from <code>oracle._attr_options</code> (the same honest domain the view oracle sweeps), shape-informed via <code>typing.shape_of</code>; a key the domain cannot honestly fill mints the bare node (undecidable beats fabricated);</li><li>the <strong>fireable pattern</strong> (<code>Candidate.rule</code>, the documented <code>as_rule</code> seam) — <code>str</code> metavar leaves plus one attr metavariable per key (<code>dim=&quot;select_dim&quot;</code>), <strong>shared across every occurrence of the op name</strong> so a match binds the real values and the RHS re-mints them — the <code>pipeline._view_node</code> convention. Ops absent from the LHS keep the instance&#39;s concrete attrs: an unbound attr metavar would fall back to the literal name string in <code>_term_instantiate</code> — a minted lie — and concrete is the one sound spelling a derive-less rule can produce.</li></ul><p>Attr key-sets are data: <code>attr_keys</code> maps op → the spellings to mint (<code>exposed_discovery</code> passes the term&#39;s own observed sets — <code>select</code> gets <code>{dim,index}</code>, <code>sum</code> gets <code>{dim}</code> <em>and</em> <code>{dim,keepdim}</code>), and the product over a pair&#39;s ops is capped at <code>_MAX_SPELLINGS=8</code>. Absent a term, <code>ATTR_SCHEMA</code> supplies the default (all declared names, plus the <code>ATTR_REQUIRED</code> subset when it differs — the elided-default shape an export may produce). Dedup moved to the <em>pattern</em> alpha-key, which also makes the library <code>relation=</code> honest for attr-bearing laws (a minted <code>select</code>-naturality can now classify <code>inverse</code> of a shipped rule instead of vacuously <code>new</code>).</p><p>The matcher itself is <strong>untouched</strong> — no wildcarding, no relaxed key-sets. <code>dim</code>/<code>index</code> stay semantics: bound by the match, re-minted into the RHS.</p><h2 id="follow-on-defect-the-fix-exposed-unbudgeted-candidates" tabindex="-1">Follow-on defect the fix exposed: unbudgeted candidates <a class="header-anchor" href="#follow-on-defect-the-fix-exposed-unbudgeted-candidates" aria-label="Permalink to “Follow-on defect the fix exposed: unbudgeted candidates”">​</a></h2><p>The moment candidates could fire, <code>proposal._cost_delta</code>&#39;s <code>[*ALL_RULES, rule]</code> saturation churned to the node cap (measured &gt;200 s where the never-firing rules ran in 0.1 s). <code>rule_budgets</code> existed for exactly this class — but only covered EXPANSIVE-tagged <em>library</em> rules. <code>proposal._rule_budgets</code> and <code>impact._rule_budgets</code> now budget every non-library rule: a candidate under test is unbounded-blast-radius by definition. Factor-left&#39;s <code>_cost_delta</code> went 200 s+ → 4 s (fixed point at ~1.8k enodes).</p><h2 id="measured-lab-screen-exposed-discovery-py-same-8-model-slice" tabindex="-1">Measured: <code>lab/screen/exposed_discovery.py</code>, same 8-model slice <a class="header-anchor" href="#measured-lab-screen-exposed-discovery-py-same-8-model-slice" aria-label="Permalink to “Measured: lab/screen/exposed_discovery.py, same 8-model slice”">​</a></h2><p>Per-model enumerate arm (<code>--evaluate 200</code>, <code>impact._probe</code> on every new+true candidate):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>model</th><th>new+true</th><th>candidates firing</th><th>total fires</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GatedAttentionUnit</td><td>12→12</td><td>0→3</td><td>0→3</td></tr><tr><td>CosineAttention</td><td>27→70</td><td>0→12</td><td>0→68</td></tr><tr><td>AdaLNBlock</td><td>20→45</td><td>0→14</td><td>0→49</td></tr><tr><td>LoRAAdapter</td><td>8→8</td><td>0→0</td><td>0→0</td></tr><tr><td>CapsuleRouting</td><td>12→11</td><td>0→1</td><td>0→2</td></tr><tr><td>ChunkedRetention</td><td>61→61</td><td>0→9</td><td>0→24</td></tr><tr><td>DeepEquilibrium</td><td>1→1</td><td>0→0</td><td>0→0</td></tr><tr><td>DeltaRuleBlock</td><td>28→24</td><td>0→5</td><td>0→52</td></tr><tr><td><strong>total</strong></td><td></td><td><strong>0→44</strong></td><td><strong>0→198</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Verified-passing fires (rule instantiated real attrs, lowered modules agree): <code>select∘sigmoid = sigmoid∘select</code> (4×, DeltaRuleBlock), <code>transpose∘relu = relu∘transpose</code> (GAU), <code>reshape∘chunk = chunk∘reshape</code> (3×, CosineAttention), <code>chunk∘unsqueeze = unsqueeze∘chunk</code> (3×, AdaLNBlock), <code>detach_∘contiguous</code> swap/inverse/absorb (ChunkedRetention), <code>unsqueeze∘select</code> swap (12×, DeltaRuleBlock). These are the op-naturality family the census arm knew from <code>mixed:*_select_*_w</code>/<code>mul_unsqueeze</code> — the enumerator now reaches them independently, as the retro predicted it should.</p><h2 id="honest-limits" tabindex="-1">Honest limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#honest-limits" aria-label="Permalink to “Honest limits”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>No paying+verified candidates.</strong> Three AdaLNBlock rows report <code>paid=True</code> but <code>verify=FAIL</code> (<code>chunk(A, chunks=1) = add(A, 0)</code> / <code>mul(1, A)</code> family): the eval draw <code>chunks=1</code> makes a <em>conditional</em> truth (<code>chunks=1 ⇒ identity</code>) look unconditional; the law is false at <code>chunks≥2</code> and the lowered-module verify correctly refuses it. The enumerate arm has no view-oracle / guard machinery — conditional truths are caught at verify, not proposed with the condition. Nothing new is shippable; nothing shipped.</li><li><strong>Same-attr sharing is narrower than the truth.</strong> Attr metavars are per-op-<em>name</em>, so two occurrences of one op in a pattern must bind equal attrs (<code>select(select x, d, i), d, i</code> misses mixed-attr nestings) — sound, but under-reaches.</li><li><strong>Eval is one draw.</strong> The instance checks the first <code>_attr_options</code> element at the (4,4) leaf shape; a law true only off the canonical draw is missed, and (above) a law true only <em>at</em> it is admitted to the probe stage, where verify disposes.</li><li><strong>Cost is real now.</strong> Bounded evals that ran ~0.1 s under never-firing rules take ~1–4 s each (LoRAAdapter&#39;s 110-eval pool took 377 s). The <code>--evaluate</code> budget is the knob.</li><li><strong>Arity wall stands.</strong> <code>concat</code>/<code>softmax</code>/<code>stack</code>/<code>einsum</code>/ <code>zeros</code>/<code>arange</code> report arity <code>None</code> and never enter the vocab — attr minting can&#39;t help ops the grammar can&#39;t spell.</li><li><strong><code>forms.py</code> shares the pre-fix defect.</strong> <code>enumerate_form_ candidates</code> instantiates the same <code>_instantiate</code> Var-leaf, attr-free way — same zero-fire exposure, not addressed here.</li><li><code>_probe</code> itself is still unbudgeted (its fire count is the reported metric); a self-feeding candidate on a real term is bounded only by <code>_FIRING_NODES</code>. Not observed to be slow.</li></ul><p>Machine-readable: <code>enum-attr-gap-before.json</code>, <code>enum-attr-gap-after.json</code> (this directory).</p>`,20)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};